{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"web_search","id":"exec-2904e9a5-730b-43b7-935c-a96da117a2c5","query":"site:prisma.io Prisma ORM 8 orm init contract emit db init postgres documentation","action":{"type":"search","query":"site:prisma.io Prisma ORM 8 orm init contract emit db init postgres documentation"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search0","snippet":"`orm init` scaffolds the Prisma 8 config, contract source, and runtime files inside an existing project, installs dependencies, and emits the contract. ... `bunx prisma@latest","title":"orm init | Prisma 8 CLI | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://docs.prisma.io/docs/cli/orm-init"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search1","snippet":"First, `orm init` installs `@prisma/orm-postgres` and `dotenv`, adding them to `package.json` if they are not there yet, and uses the installed package to check that","title":"orm init | Prisma ORM CLI | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://www.prisma.io/docs/cli/orm-init"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search2","snippet":"`orm init` scaffolds the Prisma 8 config, contract source, and runtime files inside an existing project, installs dependencies, and emits the contract. ... `bunx prisma@next","title":"orm init | Prisma 8 CLI | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://docs.prisma.io/docs/cli/v8/init"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search3","snippet":"* `capabilities`: which database features this contract can use. `npx prisma contract emit` collects them from the adapter for your database and from the packages","title":"The Prisma ORM contract files | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/contract-authoring/the-contract-artifact"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search4","snippet":"A PostgreSQL project installs two packages: `prisma`, the command-line tool, and `@prisma/orm-postgres`, the library your app imports, which includes the database driver. `npx prisma@latest orm","title":"Prisma ORM core concepts | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/core-concepts"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search5","snippet":"You describe your data in a contract, which is the file that holds your models, and Prisma ORM gives you typed queries and migrations for","title":"What is Prisma ORM? | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search6","snippet":"Run without `--db`, `db init` takes the connection from `db.connection` in `prisma.config.ts` and advances the ref named `db` to the contract it just applied. ...","title":"db init | Prisma ORM CLI | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://www.prisma.io/docs/cli/db-init"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search7","snippet":"Setup gives you the app template, a starter contract, `prisma-8.md`, project-level Prisma ORM skills for your coding agent, and package scripts for the database steps","title":"Quickstart: Prisma ORM with PostgreSQL | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://www.prisma.io/docs/prisma-orm/quickstart/postgresql"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search8","snippet":"To add Prisma 8 to a project that already uses PostgreSQL, you will run `orm init`, infer a contract from the live schema, sign the","title":"Add Prisma 8 to an existing PostgreSQL project | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://docs.prisma.io/docs/prisma-orm/add-to-existing-project/postgresql"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search9","snippet":"Update the seed script under `src/prisma/` and the app routes to query the new schema, start `npm run dev` in the background (with `DATABASE_URL` exported),","title":"Prisma ORM getting started | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://www.prisma.io/docs/getting-started"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search10","snippet":"`prisma@latest` runs Prisma ORM 8, and `--target postgres` picks PostgreSQL. `--authoring psl` picks PSL, the Prisma Schema Language, which is the `.prisma` file format you","title":"Add Prisma ORM and PostgreSQL to an existing app | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://www.prisma.io/docs/prisma-orm/quickstart/existing-app/postgresql"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.prisma.io","ref_id":"turn0search11","snippet":"`bunx prisma@next db init --db \"$DATABASE_URL\"` ... `bunx prisma@next contract emit ... Use `db update` when the database already exists and you want Prisma 8","title":"db init | Prisma 8 CLI | Prisma Documentation","url":"https://docs.prisma.io/docs/cli/v8/db-init"}]}}
